      "inverse": [
        {
          "start": 627,
          "end": 912,
          "after": "\n- Keep warm canonical Memo rejection ahead of the poisoned payer, and remove\n  query slice coercions and miss indexing through borrowed Vec/Zip receiving.\n  Complete old controls and strict paid-reduction gate remain; NEXT qualification\n  and actual application effects are pending.\n\n",
          "before": ""
        },
        {
          "start": 3148,
          "end": 3526,
          "after": "- Preserve borrowed-root hostile census checks while applying nested freeze-loan assertions to local owned storage; separate nested test-ledger backing from production refusal allocations.\n\n- Acquire the ordinary replay type-clone cursor only for payloads that can construct it, retaining owned backing charges, conservative recursive fallback and sticky payer authentication.\n\n",
          "before": ""
        },
        {
          "start": 158959,
          "end": 159430,
          "after": "\n- Share complete cleanup inventory validation with the ordinary schema summary receiver, avoiding discarded inventory storage while retaining the original materializer as an executable control. Source-only candidate; scoped runtime qualification remains pending.\n- Bind dependent invalid owned-record pattern recovery to the original declaration diagnostic, preserving independent body/mode/declaration errors. Source-only #859 candidate; focused qualification pending.\n",
          "before": ""
        },
        {
          "start": 556440,
          "end": 556816,
          "after": "\n- Source-authored #765 invocation-paid private-authority roots backing leases\n  rebuild logical roots/work on every complete caller, retain exclusive cleanup\n  guards through consumer use, and preserve independent full old receivers.\n  Zero/exact/short/floor/sticky/foreign/Drop/parity controls await qualification;\n  no measured savings or application admission is claimed.\n",
          "before": ""
        }
      ]
    },
